---
// The fortnight menu editor's markup (docs/meal-plan.md), on both ForkKnife's Spoon Feed page and FortKnight's Build
// page: the rules in prose, a status line, and the container the per-meal sections are drawn into by
// lib/meal-plan-editor.js. Which face the page belongs to only changes where the "or let your assistant draft it"
// link points — either Assistant page applies a meal-plan document, because the profile is shared.
import { facePath } from "../lib/faces.js";

const { face } = Astro.props;
---
<fieldset data-section="menu">
  <legend>Your fortnight menu</legend>
  <p class="muted">For each meal, add the dishes and the days you eat them. The first day is the fresh serving; the second is leftovers. Leftovers are never eaten the next day, and never more than three days later — the fortnight wraps, so Monday B follows Saturday B. Leftovers of an afternoon or evening meal can also become an earlier meal: dinner on Sunday A can be breakfast on Tuesday A. About eight dishes cover a meal’s fourteen days, and a meal takes one dish a day. The meals themselves — their names, when you eat them, whether they need prepping or cooking — are ForkKnife’s <a href={facePath("forkknife", "questionnaire/")}>Questionnaire</a>. Or let your assistant draft the whole menu on the <a href={facePath(face, "assistant/")}>Assistant page</a>.</p>
  <p class="muted" id="planStatus"></p>
  <div id="mealSections"></div>
</fieldset>
